                    #modalAuthDenial.modal(role="dialog")
                        .modal__dialog.modal__dialog--w600
                            .modal__body
                                p
                                    strong ESSOAr collects your iD from ORCID for use in our systems to:
                                ul
                                    li Streamline the sign up / log in process – so you don’t have to remember one more user name and password!
                                    li Reduce time form-filling.
                                p You must be signed into your account with your ORCID credentials to submit content to ESSOAr, or to access your Author or Advisor Dashboard.
                                p In the future, we can also push your affiliation with ESSOAr to your ORCID record. You may later revoke permissions on your account settings page, if you choose.
                                p If you don’t connect your ORCID iD with ESSOAr, you will not be able to proceed.

